<title>UK: TABLE-NatWest H1 pretax rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NatWest H1 pretax rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997 (million stg unless stated)  Shr (pence)		28.5	   vs 6.3 loss</p>
<p> Headline earnings/shr  30.0	   vs 33.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 10.6	   vs 9.6</p>
<p> Pretax from cont ops   775	    vs 662</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    669	    vs 302</p>
<p> Group balance sheet    8,025	  vs 7,791</p>
<p> Operating income	 3,539	  vs 3,346</p>
<p> Trading surplus	  1,054	  vs 1,048</p>
<p> Provisions		 270	    vs 270</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British bank is National Westminster Bank Plc. Analysts had forecast pretax profits between 757 million stg and 770 million stg and a dividend between 10.4 pence and 11 pence. The profit before tax from continuing operations is before a charge of 106 million stg for the impact of the corporation tax change on finance leases, the bank said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
